# RULESET: Furniture WMS Development Guidelines
# Reference Document: SRS_Furniture_WMS.md

## 1. Context & Architecture
- Build a Warehouse Management System for Furniture with AI integration based on SRS_Furniture_WMS.md.
- Architecture: Layered Architecture (Controller -> Service -> Domain -> Repository/DAL).
- Single Source of Truth for stock: `stock_ledger` table. Never modify stock directly without going through the Inventory Service.

## 2. Strict Business Rules
- CBM Calculation: Calculate CBM automatically: `CBM = (length_mm * width_mm * height_mm) / 1,000,000,000`. Validate all 3 dimensions > 0.
- Combo/BOM Stock: Do NOT store static stock for Combo items. Calculate dynamically: `MIN(floor(available_stock[i] / qty_per_set[i]))`.
- Stock Status: Always distinguish `GOOD` and `DAMAGED` stock. Available stock for sales MUST exclude `DAMAGED` items.

## 3. Concurrency & Locking Rules (Pessimistic Locking)
- All operations modifying stock balance MUST use Pessimistic Locking (`SELECT ... FOR UPDATE`).
- Multi-item locking (Combos or Transfers) MUST sort items by `sku_id` or `warehouse_id` ASCENDING before locking to prevent deadlocks.
- Set `lock_timeout` (default 5-10s). Handle lock acquisition failure with error code `ERR-LOCK-001`.

## 4. Security & Audit
- Enforce Role-Based Access Control (RBAC) on every API endpoint.
- Every CUD action on business entities MUST generate an entry in `audit_log`.
- AI Engine operates in READ-ONLY mode. Proposals require human approval (`APPROVED` status) before creating official records.